    "answer": {
      "short": "32 complete trains. $90\\div\\frac{11}{4}=32\\frac{8}{11}$, so the next train is unfinished.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Time available}&=1\\frac{1}{2}\\times60\\\\&=90\\text{ minutes}\\\\\\text{Number of trains}&=90\\div2\\frac{3}{4}\\\\&=90\\div\\frac{11}{4}\\\\&=\\frac{90}{1}\\times\\frac{4}{11}\\\\&=\\frac{360}{11}\\\\&=32\\frac{8}{11}\\end{align*}$$\n\nJames can assemble 32 complete trains; there is insufficient time to finish the next train.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
